---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { NavigationMenuPlayground, NavigationMenuSiteHeader } from '../../components/NavigationMenuDemo';
---

<Docs title="Navigation Menu" description="A row of site links where some items open a panel of more links.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Navigation Menu</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A row of site links. Some items are plain links; others open a panel of more links. Every panel shares one popup
    that resizes and slides as you move between triggers.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="navigation-menu-demo">
    <NavigationMenuPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Navigation menu usage"
      code={`import {
  NavigationMenu,
  NavigationMenuContent,
  NavigationMenuItem,
  NavigationMenuLink,
  NavigationMenuList,
  NavigationMenuTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/navigation-menu";

<NavigationMenu>
  <NavigationMenuList>
    <NavigationMenuItem>
      <NavigationMenuTrigger>Projects</NavigationMenuTrigger>
      <NavigationMenuContent>
        <div className="grid w-56 gap-0.5 p-1">
          <NavigationMenuLink href="/projects/meadow">Meadow project</NavigationMenuLink>
          <NavigationMenuLink href="/projects/garden">Garden notes</NavigationMenuLink>
        </div>
      </NavigationMenuContent>
    </NavigationMenuItem>
    <NavigationMenuItem>
      <NavigationMenuLink href="/help">Help</NavigationMenuLink>
    </NavigationMenuItem>
  </NavigationMenuList>
</NavigationMenu>`}
    />
    <p>
      An item holds either a <code>NavigationMenuTrigger</code> with its <code>NavigationMenuContent</code>, or a single{' '}
      <code>NavigationMenuLink</code>. Top-level links get the same 32px height as triggers. Set the panel width on the
      content you put inside it; the popup sizes itself to fit.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Site header</h2>
    <p>
      Panels can hold anything: a list of links with icons and descriptions, or a two-column grid that drops to one
      column on narrow screens. Pass <code>active</code> to mark the current page. Add{' '}
      <code>NavigationMenuIndicator</code> after a trigger for a pointer under the open item, and use{' '}
      <code>navigationMenuTriggerStyle()</code> to give any link the trigger look. Disabled triggers are skipped by
      pointer and dimmed.
    </p>
    <NavigationMenuSiteHeader client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="navigation-menu-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>NavigationMenu</code> wraps the Base UI navigation menu root and renders the shared popup for you. It takes{' '}
      <code>align</code> (<code>"start"</code>, <code>"center"</code>, or <code>"end"</code>; default{' '}
      <code>"start"</code>), <code>value</code>, <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onValueChange</code>,{' '}
      <code>delay</code>, <code>closeDelay</code>, and every <code>nav</code>
      prop.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>NavigationMenuTrigger</code> takes <code>disabled</code> and adds a chevron that turns while its panel is
      open. <code>NavigationMenuContent</code> takes
      <code>keepMounted</code>. <code>NavigationMenuLink</code> takes <code>active</code> (sets{' '}
      <code>aria-current="page"</code>), <code>closeOnClick</code> (default
      <code>false</code>), and <code>render</code> for your router link.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>NavigationMenuPositioner</code> is the portal, positioner, popup, and viewport. The root already renders one
      with <code>side="bottom"</code>, <code>sideOffset</code> 8, <code>alignOffset</code> 0, and{' '}
      <code>collisionPadding</code> 8; use it directly only when composing a root by hand. Each part sets a
      <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The root is a <code>nav</code>; give it an <code>aria-label</code> when a page has more than one. Tab moves
      between items. Enter, Space, or Arrow Down opens a panel and moves focus into it; arrow keys move between links;
      Escape closes the panel and returns focus to its trigger. Panels also open on hover after a short delay.
    </p>
    <p>
      The popup fades and scales over 120ms, and resizes and slides between panels over 180ms. Motion turns off when
      reduced motion is requested. In forced-colors mode the popup keeps a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Navigation menus use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code>--sprout-active</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the control and panel radii. They need no
      brand color, so they look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
